<main class="case-page">
<section class="case-hero"><a class="back-link" href="../../">← Back to portfolio</a><div class="case-identity"><div><p class="eyebrow">PURCHASING · SUPPLIERS · QUOTES</p><span class="status status--internal">INTERNAL USE</span><h1>Purchasing and Quotes</h1><p class="case-category">From request to supplier follow-up</p><p class="case-summary">I built a desktop application to organize purchase requests, supplier quotes and replies. Instead of tracking every step in separate spreadsheets and emails, the team can work through one flow from the request to the response.</p></div><div class="case-hero__visual"><figure class="case-showcase"><div class="case-showcase__frame"><img src="../../../assets/evidence/compras-painel-inicial.png" alt="Demonstration screen with options to create purchase requests and find suppliers." loading="eager" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><span class="evidence-label">REAL INTERFACE · DEMONSTRATION DATA</span><strong>One place to start common purchase requests.</strong></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>
<section class="case-facts" aria-label="Overview"><div><span>Where it is used</span><b>Purchasing operations</b></div><div><span>What it organizes</span><b>Suppliers · requests · quotes · replies</b></div><div><span>Key safeguard</span><b>Review before sending</b></div></section>
<section class="case-gallery-section"><div class="case-gallery-heading"><p>IN DAILY USE</p><h2>Prepare and follow up</h2><span>The team organizes request details and tracks replies without searching through separate email threads.</span></div><div class="case-gallery"><figure class="case-gallery__item"><div class="case-gallery__frame"><img src="../../../assets/evidence/compras-cotacao-frete.png" alt="Demonstration form for requesting a freight quote." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><span class="evidence-label">QUOTE</span><strong>Cargo details and recipients on one screen.</strong></figcaption></figure><figure class="case-gallery__item"><div class="case-gallery__frame"><img src="../../../assets/evidence/compras-acompanhamento.png" alt="Screen for tracking supplier replies and open actions." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><span class="evidence-label">FOLLOW-UP</span><strong>Replies and next steps in the same workflow.</strong></figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="case-story"><article><span>01</span><h2>The problem</h2><p>Supplier details, requests, attachments and replies were spread across spreadsheets, emails and messages. It was hard to find a contact and tell who had responded.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h2>What I built</h2><p>I created a Windows application to search suppliers, prepare quote requests and purchase orders, review outgoing messages and track replies.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h2>How it works</h2><p>A person chooses the request type, enters the necessary details, checks recipients and attachments, and then sends it. The application organizes replies and shows what still needs attention.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h2>Who uses it</h2><p>The tool supports the purchasing team when supplier quotes are needed.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h2>The benefit</h2><p>Requests, messages and replies stay connected. The team spends less time switching between files and emails and can pick up follow-up work more easily.</p></article><article><span>06</span><h2>The challenge</h2><p>The app needs to handle replies that arrive later and temporary email failures. It keeps local history and a queue so work can resume safely.</p></article></section>
<section class="case-limit"><div><p class="eyebrow">Technology</p><p>Python · PySide6 · SQLite · IMAP/SMTP · Excel · Windows.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Public demo</p><p>The screens use fictional data. Sending and network synchronization are disabled in this version; no supplier or company document is published.</p></div></section>
<section class="case-proof"><p>I built the tool around a real purchasing workflow and continue to evolve it with the people who use it.</p></section>
